  "description": "IQETUT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H168 Ce4 N12 O26. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.656-3.972 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.79-131.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Ce4(μ3-O)2(O2CNiPr2)12. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
